	<key>CBReleaseHotfixes</key>
	<string>Timed-out SSH health probes were shown as online with an empty readout; they now correctly report the host as down.
A hung network or FUSE mount no longer freezes a host’s whole health check — disk stats are capped at 5s.</string>
	<key>CBReleaseKnownIssues</key>
	<string>Claude status is checked only while AI Bar is open — it is not a 24/7 watch.
Don’t run AI Bar and Claude Bar at the same time — they share one backend socket and account lock.</string>
	<key>CBReleaseWhatsNew</key>
	<string>Server monitor reliability: a stuck host now shows red instead of a misleading green dot with no data.
Health checks stay responsive even when a disk mount stalls, so the rest of a host’s stats still load.</string>
